# tools/history-scan.mjs: matches that are not findings. One regex per line, tested against the matched text.
# Synthetic strings in the gates' own tests and fixtures only. A real name, path or address never goes here: this file
# is public, and a line here switches a gate off for that string.
#
# the home-path gate's own test fixtures, and URL paths that look like home folders
^/home/(alice|static|page|owner)$
^/tmp/claude$
^/Users/c$
^C:\\\\Users\\\\B$
# the noise tools/history-scan.mjs documents and tests
^Q@B\.csJ$
# reserved example addresses (RFC 2606), and the trailer every Claude-assisted commit carries
@example\.(com|org)$
^noreply@anthropic\.com$
# the private-source tests: made-up account: addresses, so a real one still fails
account:(supplier-chat|zeta|shop|mail|chat)/
account:x\b
# the identity the public mirror commits with (tools/public-export.mjs): GitHub's address that goes nowhere
@users\.noreply\.github\.com$
# phone numbers reserved for fiction (North America's 555-0100 to 0199, Ofcom's 020 7946 0xxx), and a made-up address
^\+1 \d{3} 555 01\d\d$
^\+1 \(\d{3}\) 555-01\d\d$
^\+44 20 7946 0\d{3}$
^a@b\.co$
